#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2260 expect=skipped domain=TS
#note "K4-DICT no-dictionary SKIP pin (unii, once per dictionary type). Violating-shaped data (row 2 TRT|NOTADRUG would fire) but `#dictionaries` is DELIBERATELY ABSENT, so the rule MUST report SKIPPED even though the TSPARMCD conjunct is evaluable, never a false PASS. Mechanism (stage-R escalation triage 2026-08-20, read at source): NO shipped rule carries a dictionary_available(<type>) Precondition. OperationInliner.addLibraryPreconditionGate (lib/corej-rules/src/main/java/net/cumba/corej/core/expr/convert/OperationInliner.java:862-921) emits the gate only for INLINED operations, and no dictionary operation is inlined anywhere in lib/corej-rules/rules/ (98 rules keep the declared $-ref form; the corpus has ZERO Preconditions), while RuleRunner's eager provider-absence skip loop (lib/corej-core/src/main/java/net/cumba/corej/core/exec/RuleRunner.java:644-677) has arms for isLibraryDependent and isDefineDependent but NONE for isDictionaryDependent. With no provider the operation returns null (OperationExecutor.java:2059-2066 / :2119-2126) and the null operand fires no row, so the rule EXECUTES and reports noViolation - a false PASS. The harness no-provider mode is NOT the problem: AbstractRuleTestSuitesFactory.resolveDictionaries:842-848 correctly returns null when #dictionaries is absent. ENGINE DEFECT (EC-ledger candidate); this pin is RED IN-TREE AS D9 EVIDENCE and goes green when the declared-form dictionary skip gate lands."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TSSEQ    type=Num
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
---
S01 | TS | 1 | TRT | ASPIRIN
S01 | TS | 2 | TRT | NOTADRUG
